# RXSky three-basis v02

- Source: current `/Game/UltraDynamicSky/Maps/DemoMap`, `Ultra_Dynamic_Sky.VolumetricCloud`. This is the user's UDS cloud source, not the preceding VDB layout.
- Result: `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/Maps/L_RXSkySystem_ThreeBasis_v02`.
- Parameter source: saved `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/Maps/L_RXSkySystem_ThreeBasis`. All 115 editable sky properties were copied and compared for equality before replacing the cloned actor; time is 10.368. Sky/cloud component transforms and visibility were retained.
- Isolated BP/MI: `Cubeless/ThreeBasis/v02/BP_RXSkySystem_ThreeBasis_v02` and `Materials/MI_Clouds_ThreeBasis_v02`. Approved corrected cloud parent is shared. Earlier result assets were not replaced.
- Texture: `Baking/Bakes/Cubeless_UDS_Beauty45_v02_20260920/T_Cubeless_UDS_Beauty45_v02_20260920_Beauty45_RGBA`.

## Capture

4096 linear HDR RGBA: R upper45, G lower45, B back, A coverage. Six 2048 faces with eight samples per pass, 192 sequential captures. Bounded cubeless quality profile retained. UDS collection values were frozen into an isolated collection; source instance texture/static settings were copied. Isolated transport/coverage materials use original density, isotropic phase, white transport albedo, zero ambient/emission, and extinction-driven coverage emission. Original UDS assets were not edited. Source scene primitives/lights were temporarily hidden, with a transient capture light/camera; state restoration passed and the source level was saved after restoration.

The runtime result uses pixels only and has no UDS or MCP dependency from the baked texture. Three fixed global lighting directions retain the known lateral-relighting limitation. Existing ground cloud-shadow material remains inherited from the previous result; this task replaces the visible cloud dome bake.

## Verification

- Bake completed; restoration reports no errors. Coverage range 0–0.9956; finite directional RGB values.
- Result BP compiled with zero errors/warnings; all 115 editable values matched.
- Live CloudBasis readback resolves to the v02 texture. Map saved and open in the editor.
- Direct dependency audit passed for map, BP, MI and texture with no MCP references.
- Visual evidence: `Saved/RXThreeBasisDome/v02_result.png`.
- Parameter evidence: `Saved/RXThreeBasisDome/v02/applied.json`.
- Bake report: `Saved/RXSkyBaking/Cubeless_UDS_Beauty45_v02_20260920/bake.json`.
- Full offline profile passed all 42 checks: `Saved/RXThreeBasisDome/v02_full.log`.

Editor-only helpers: `scripts/rx_uds_three_basis_v02_capture.py`, `scripts/apply_rx_three_basis_v02_ue.py`. No project C++ changes.

## Active v02 scene fog follow-up

v02 is the forward working version; v01 remains a comparison. Isolated `M_Sky_SceneFog_v02` and `M_Clouds_SceneFog_v02` now use Before DOF, Apply Fogging and Compute Fog Per Pixel. Removed their final custom height-colour blend to avoid applying fog twice. The old CloudHorizonFog controls no longer drive these materials; scene FogDensity, FogHeightFalloff, FogExtinction and FogViewDistance are the active fog controls. Other artist colour grading remains.

`MI_Clouds_SceneFog_v02` replaces the original v02 instance in UpdateSky. `MI_CloudShadow_v02` uses the new RGBA texture's alpha through Positive, replacing the inherited previous bake. Native fog revealed excessive forward light at SunVolumeStrength 15.36: the placed v02 actor now uses 1.0 and FogAnisotropy 0.65. Time restored to 8.064; level saved. New BP instances retain their existing default values unless overridden.

The initial attempt to reparent the live instance during shader compilation caused a UE UniformExpressionCache assertion and editor exit. No new material assets had been saved at that point. Editor was relaunched; corrected authoring creates and finishes compilation of isolated parents before connecting a new instance, leaving the live old parent untouched. Material/BP compilation succeeded; direct dependency audit passed. Evidence: `v02_native_fog.png`, `v02_fog_balanced.png`, `v02_volume_off.png`, `v02_fog_full.log` under Saved/RXThreeBasisDome. Helper: `scripts/fix_rx_v02_scene_fog_ue.py`.

### Horizon opacity and dome-distance correction

Follow-up inspection found the placed CloudDome at relative scale 0.04865075 while SkyDome was scale 1 with a translated centre. Aligning both transforms alone did not remove the bright horizon cloud strip. The decisive restriction was ExponentialHeightFog `fog_max_opacity=0.28`: analytic height fog could retain at least 72% of source colour even at long distance. Raising this to 0.98 visibly faded the lowest clouds into the surrounding fog. Both component templates and the placed actor now have aligned dome transforms and maximum fog opacity 0.98. UpdateSky readback preserves these values, and BP/level were saved. Existing density, falloff and cloud colours were retained. Evidence: `v02_fog_distance_fixed.png` (alignment only), `v02_fog_opacity_fixed.png` (opacity correction), and `v02_fog_opacity_full.log` under Saved/RXThreeBasisDome.
